rozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 94 at 07 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   is a 375 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm simple mastectomy specimen covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm triangular skin ellipse with a centrally placed 0 8cm unremarkable nipple  The breast is oriented with a short suture marking the superior and a long stitch marking the lateral skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white  firm  irregular stellate mass with a central 1 5cm rock hard  tan area that extends 0 5cm deep and 3 0cm medially to the nipple  The mass extends 0 3cm to the closest deep margin  abuts the inferior margin  and to within 0 5cm from the skin and 2 0cm from the superior margin  There is an adjacent tan white  rubbery  fibrous area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm adjacent to the breast mass extending 2 0cm laterally  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A B  mass with closest deep margin  D E  mass with closest inferior margin  F  mass with adjacent inferior margin  G  overlying skin adjacent to mass  H  more portion of section in cassette G  including deep margin  I  representative sections of superior margin  J  representative section of 