 for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 13 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast lumpectomy  is a 6 x 4 x 2 5cm fibrofatty tissue with a long stitch designating medial and a short stitch designating superior  The specimen is already inked by the surgeon as follows  superior in yellow  deep in green  inferior in blue  and anterior in orange  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm gritty nodule is present 0 3cm from the medial margin  Also identified is a 1 x 1 x 0 2cm ill defined firm area  which is adjacent to a clip and abuts the anterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominately fatty  The entire small nodule and a representative section of the firm area are frozen as FX 1  now in cassette A  Additional representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes B L  area adjacent to the small nodule is in C  the firm area in F   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  additional medial margin  is a 2 x 1 x 0 2cm fatty tissue with slight nodularity  The specimen is entirely frozen as FX 2  now in cassette M  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number are three parts  Labeled  left breast final margin  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of breast with