his laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three separate containers  Labeled  right breast and right axillary contents  lymphadenectomy Level I  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm overlying skin ellipse and a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm inverted nipple  centered on a 2 0cm in diameter ill defined areola  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm white to focally yellow granular stellate mass that extends to within 2 5cm of the closest inked resection margin  Anteriorly the mass extends to reach the overlying skin in the nipple area  focally showing paste like consistency  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  AandB  tumor and closest resection margin C F  tumor G I  unremarkable breast parenchyma J N  representative lymph nodes  Labeled  right axillary lymphadenectomy Level II  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  represenative lymmph nodes submitted in O and P  Labeled  right axilla  Hot spot  1  Ct 90  is an aggregate of fibroadipose tissue  A representative lymph node is submitted in cassette Q  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  LEVEL 2 PART C  RIGHT AXILARY LYMP