ctomy specimen containing a REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm nipple and a REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm areola on the anterior surface  A long stitch designates the superior aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  and posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a firm fibrous breast parenchyma with an area of granular  firm discoloration in the medial portion of the breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  with ill defined borders  Photographs are taken  Representative sections from this ill defined area are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In addition  a nodular yellow tan mass is present in the anterior inferior breast  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and located 0 6cm from the anterior margin and 1 5cm from the posterior margin  The nodule incised to reveal a cyst containing clear serous fluid  The nodule is entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable  Representative sections from normal appearing breast are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Gross Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael W Lawlor M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor