 tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 12 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast biopsy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm tan yellow  well delineated nodule with white streaks  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved as frozen  The remaining nodule entirely in A through E  representative sections of the remaining tissue  greater than 95   in F through L  Gross Description by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
