 in situ  present  No definite tumor mass was appreciated on gross exam  however  invasive tumor is present in 5 of 5 representative sections of the healing biopsy site and measures at least 2 2cm in maximum diameter microscopically  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Her 2 only   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  20 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  22 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Extracapsular extension  Marked Other forms of axillary involvement  None Method of detection  Both hematoxylin and eosin and cytokeratin immunohistochemistry  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 6 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  sentinel nodes right axilla hot   blue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm yellow soft tissue  dissected to reveal 3 lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Largest node is inked black and bisected and the lymph nodes frozen entirely as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining tissue is submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  additional margin right breast   is an unoriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing multiple lymph nodes  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes  both bisected  1 of which is