e the presence of myoepithelial cells around the foci of in situ and not the invasive carcinoma  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MEDIAL INFERIOR MARGINS   EXCISION  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  An e cadherin stain does not support the presence of lobular neoplasia  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  LATERAL HALF OF CAVITY   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  MEDIAL HALF OF CAVITY   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE REMOVED_DATE OUT OF 3  SPANNING AT LEAST 0 5CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  PRESENT ON AT LEAST 4 OUT OF 7 SLIDES  SEE NOTE  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FLORID USUAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  There are small foci of extruded mucin which are suspicious for the presence of invasive carcinoma  however  the possibility that these foci represent artifactual rupture of mucin into the stroma cannot be entirely excluded  In one focus  myoepithelial markers  calponin  p63  and myosin  are helpful in establishing the presence of in situ carcinoma  In another focus  however  the area of concern is not present on deeper levels  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 5 OUT OF 5 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on six  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mammographic localization   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm breast excision specimen oriented with a short stitch on its superior edge  and a long stitch on its lateral edge  The long axis of the specimen is superior inferior and the specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  There are two needle localization wires entering the specimen on its anterior inferior surface which mark two masses  one adjacent to the hook and thick segment of the wires  and the other located 1cm medial and superior to the hook and thick segment of the wire  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the following axis to demonstrate two palpable masses measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm respectively  The first mass  1 o clock  is 1 2cm from the superior margin  1 6cm from the inferior margin  0 3cm from the posterior margin  0 7cm from the anterior margin  1 3cm from the lateral margin  and  2cm from the medial margin  The second mass  probable 2 o clock  is located 1 5cm from the superior margin  1 0cm from the inferior margin  1 1cm from the anterior margin  1 2cm from the lateral margin   2cm from the medial margin  and abuts the posterior margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections of the first mass with respect to nearest margins are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the second mass with respect to the nearest margins are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The superior margin with grossly unremarkable breast tissue is submitted enface as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The inferior margin with grossly unremarkable breast tissue is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional deep medial inferior tissue   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of breast tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal grossly unremarkable breast tissue  The specimen is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin lateral one half of cavity   is an aggregate of unoriented breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The specimen is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin medial one half of cavity   is an unoriented aggregate of fatty breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimen is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node left axilla hot and blue   REMOVED_CASE_ID   781   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fatty tissue which is dissected to reveal five potential lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 6cm to 0 9cm in greatest diameter  The lymph nodes are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Pavan K Auluck M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Pavan K Auluck M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MEDIAL INFERIOR MARGINS   EXCI PART C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL REMOVED_DATE OF