h a pink granular lining and areas of more densely fibrous and retracted tissue around the biopsy cavity  Also noted is white packing material filling throughout the biopsy cavity  The parenchyma is primarily adipose  with a diffuse scattering of more fibrous areas  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  radially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from lateral to medial  including all margins  the biopsy cavity  and representative denser regions   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end  radially  Received fresh  labeled  superior medial left breast margin   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of breast tissue which is oriented with a stitch at the new margin  The specimen is partially fragmented as received  Parts of the specimen clearly belonging to the aspect marked with the stitch are inked in black  Ten representative radial sections to the new margin are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  inferior left breast margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of breast tissue with a stitch designating the new margin  The aspect marked with the stitch is inked black per protocol  Representative sections to the inked margins are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  more medial left breast margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm grossly unremarkable breast tissue specimen with the new margin oriented with the stitch  The oriented new margin is inked black per protocol  The specimen is sectioned radially to the inked margin and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1 AND 1A   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE  EXCISION   ONE  1  LYMPH NODE  NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  R