Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 59 CLINICAL DATA                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE LATERAL AND ANTERIOR MARGINS   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE ANTERIOR AND LATERAL MARGINS  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  RADIAL SCARS  MICROSCOPIC  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  14  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT  RE EXCISION   INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCALLY ATYPICAL  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  ALL  14  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODE   ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA    EXCISION  ONE LYMPH NODE IS FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 36                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Seven specimens are received  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm incision of breast biopsy with long suture designating lateral and short suture designating superior aspect  The specimen is inked as follows  Inferior is yellow  superior is red  lateral is blue  medial is green  anterior and posterior are black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm stellate gritty mass present at the anterior margin and 0 2cm from the posterior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  Mass is submitted in cassettes A through C with anterior  black   lateral  blue   and posterior  black overinked in yellow   Needle localization site  slightly firm no gross tumor  and anterior margin are submitted in D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are the 6 remaining specimens  Labeled as  left breast  additional anterior medial margin  is an unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with focal fibrocystic changes  submitted entirely in cassettes E through J  Labeled as  left breast  final shaved margins  are three fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  They are inked and sectioned to reveal fibroadipose tissue with focal cystic changes  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes K  L and M  Labeled as  left axillary contents  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple lymph nodes are extracted  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 7cm in greatest dimension  submitted in N through S  Labeled as  reexcision  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse containing a 4 8cm well healed  linear scar  There is a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  and a short stitch designating the superior aspect which is inked in blue  while the inferior aspect is inked in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with an associated area of stellate fibrosis measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and extending to the superior and inferior margins  Posterior to the biopsy cavity is a rubbery  tan white  nodular mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and present at superior  inferior and posterior margins  The biopsy cavity itself is 0 2cm from the nearest  inferior  margin  Section code  T W  Biopsy cavity  nearest margin in W  lateral to medial X Y  Adjacent fibrous areas Z  Uninvolved parenchyma Designated right axillary contents is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which several node like structures have been extracted ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm in greatest dimension and submitted in cassettes AA through DD  Labeled as  additional axillary tissue  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which several node like structures have been extracted ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in greatest dimension submitted entirely in cassette EE  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES   ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLA    EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN    EZXCIS PART G  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION   report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Breast CTR Surg WAC 240 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  CONNIE ROCHE  NP KENNY C LAI  M D  RACHEL ANN HITT  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 56 year old woman with very dense breast with indeterminate focus of enhancement seen in the medial left breast on MRI  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  DCIS   MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SEE NOTE  Note  Sections of the core biopsy reveal a rare cluster of angulated ducts infiltrating the stroma which are present over an area measuring approximately 0 2cm  Adjacent to the lesion is a 0 3cm cluster of ducts which are expanded by a proliferation of monomorphic ductal cells arranged in a micropapillary pattern lining the duct structures  The morphologic findings are compatible with a diagnosis of invasive tubular carcinoma arising in association with low grade micropapillary ductal carcinoma in situ  To help confirm these diagnoses  we performed level sections and a panel of immunostains on the core biopsy  Multiple level sections show the DCIS to better advantage  An immunostain for keratin REMOVED_DATE shows focal loss of staining in luminal cells and supports the diagnosis of DCIS  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  demonstrate absence of the myoepithelial layer in the infiltrating ducts and supports the diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma  Overall  the findings are limited due to limited sampling of the lesion  however  based on morphology and immunohistochemistry  the findings are compatible with well differentiated invasive ductal carcinoma and low grade ductal carcinoma in situ  Dr  David Wilbur has reviewed this case and concurs with the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  aggregate of multiple tan yellow to gray white fibroadipose tissue cores  which are submitted in toto  in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday August 31   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 51 13PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left    Core biopsy  report_end  , Unknown.
