Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 00 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SPECIMEN  1  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SEVERAL NODULES RANGING BETWEEN REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  INVOLVING THE ANTERIOR AND POSTERIOR MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The nodules of invasive carcinoma probably aggregate to about 1 5cm  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SMALL FOCUS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  LEVEL I   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 13 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  LEVEL II   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   HOT SPOT  CT  REMOVED_CASE_ID    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and un it number  are five separate parts  Labeled  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast biopsy  two short suture designating the superior aspect  a long suture designating the lateral aspect  The specimen is inked black  with anterior  superficial  surface inked blue over black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal white  firm  dense tissue  most adjacent to the superior and lateral resection margins  The area of firmness has irregular  stellate configuration scattered with white spicules and measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in maximal cross section  Section code  A H  representative sections  from medial to lateral Labeled  left breast tissue  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of breast tissue  The tissue is oriented with a short stitch designating its superomedial portion  a long stitch designating the inferolateral aspect and a double stitch designating the superior aspect  that represents the new resection margin  The new resection margin is inked black  the opposite surface  adjacent to the previous specimen is inked blue  Sectioning through the specimen reveals at least three  white firm and spiculated areas  one closest to the superomedial end  abutting the superior  new  resection margin  measuring 1 5cm in maximal diameter  A separate area of firmness  measuring 0 5cm in maximal diameter is located in the deep portion of the specimen  adjacent to the superior  new  resection margin  A third irregular area of white  firm tissue is located near the inferolateral resection margin  closest to the deep resection margin  blue ink   Section code  I O  representative sections  from superomedial to inferolateral with first area of firmness in I and J  intermediate area of firmness in K through M  and inferolateral area of firmness in N and O  Labeled  left axillary lymph nodes  Level I  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm mass of adipose and fibrous tissue  Lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in P through S  Labeled  left axillary lymph nodes  Level II  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm aggregate of adipose tissue  containing few lymph nodes  Submitted entirely in T and U  labeled  left axilla  hot spot  1  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm aggregate of adipose tissue  containing at least one large lymph node  Dissected and submitted entirely in V through X  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEVEL 1  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART D  LYMPH NODES  LEVEL II  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY HOT SPOT   EXCISION   report_end  , Positive.
