  firm area noted at the 12 00 position in the central aspect of the breast  which closely approximates to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1 cm  firm to hard  tan white nodule  that is located 1 3cm from the closest posterior margin  The axillary tail is dissected for lymph nodes  with multiple potential nodes identified  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections of first tumor nodule  including anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   intervening breast parenchyma between two tumor nodules   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   second tumor nodule to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections of the second tumor nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections of the posterior margin adjacent to the second tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   sections from the nodular region with cysts  central breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections from the hard nodule  posterior central breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative section of tissue away from described lesions   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   one lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   three potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   seven potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   one lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   posterior margin in relationship to the central ill defined lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   additional potential axillary nodes  one node bisected in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and additional right axillary tissue  are fragments of tan pink pieces of soft tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Ravi M Rao M B   B C H   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Rema A Rao M D   B S   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Fin