Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  FIBROADENOMA  INVOLUTED  WITH EXTENSIVE MICROCALCIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  A   RIGHT   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS  CYSTS  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  AND EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  B   RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  60    WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE MM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  40    SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma extends to an inked margin  Definite lymphatic invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  David Weissmann  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 21 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  SPECIMEN  B    THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  with a localizing wire and x ray showing clusters of coarse calcifications at one margin  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an area of white gray  gritty tissue  abutting an inked margin  0 4 x 0 2cm    No frozen section done  Suspicious areas in cassettes A through C  rest in D through I  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled   1  right breast specimen A  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place and x ray demonstrating clusters of large coarse calcifications  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm cluster of white gray gritty material abutting an inked margin  No frozen section done  The specimen is too small to freeze  Lesion submitted in cassettes J  K and the remainder submitted entirely in cassettes L through Q  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast  B  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  an x ray demonstrating vague radio density at one end of the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a gray pink gritty fairly well circumscribed nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm extending to within 0 2cm of the inked margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable  The lesion is submitted in cassettes R through V  the remainder is submitted entirey in cassettes W through GG  No frozen done  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT   NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST A  BIOPSY  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST B  BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Simon Bergman  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST PART B  RIGHT BREAST A PART C  RIGHT BREAST B   report_end  , Positive.
